{"name":"Hidden Mask","hex":"#96748a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hidden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of hide"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Located or positioned out of sight; not visually apparent.","Obscure. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hidden"},{"term":"mask","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cover, or partial cover, for the face, used for disguise or protection.","That which disguises; a pretext or subterfuge."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover (the face or something else), in order to conceal the identity or protect against injury; to cover with a mask or visor.","To disguise as something else."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mask"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mask","blocks":[{"text":"A mask is an object normally worn on the face, typically for protection, disguise, performance, or entertainment, and often employed for rituals and rites. Masks have been used since antiquity for both ceremonial and practical purposes, as well as in the performing arts and for entertainment. They are usually worn on the face, though they may also be positioned elsewhere on the wearer's body for effect."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Ravensburg_Fasnet_Papierkrattler_2005.jpg/330px-Ravensburg_Fasnet_Papierkrattler_2005.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mask","wikidata":"Q161524"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/MaskOfAgamemnon.jpg/500px-MaskOfAgamemnon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c8/MaskOfAgamemnon.jpg/1280px-MaskOfAgamemnon.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/th